    "updated_at": "2015-09-02T11:25:02Z",
    "body": "> If it's used by authors but doesn't have implementation any requirements, does it need to be mentioned?\n\nJust FYI: For any elements or attributes listed in this section, we have code in the validator ([here](https://github.com/validator/validator/blob/master/src/nu/validator/checker/schematronequiv/Assertions.java#L1141) and [here](https://github.com/validator/validator/blob/master/src/nu/validator/checker/schematronequiv/Assertions.java#L1511)) that instead of just emitting a generic _This is invalid_ message for that error/attribute, emits a special message of the form, `The foo attribute on the bar element is obsolete. Use CSS instead.` (and a similar message for any obsolete element), were the `Use CSS instead` part varies based on what the spec actually says the suggested alternative to the obsolete element/attribute is.\n\nSo in practice it does affect more than just authors.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
