    "created_at": "2015-09-02T15:00:21Z",
    "updated_at": "2015-09-02T15:00:21Z",
    "body": "> So should `<event-source>` be mentioned?\n\nI think it should be if it was ever used in deployed content on the Web (which it was, right?).\n\nI think that should actually be the general rule: If there is deployed content out there on some kind of scale that contains an element or attribute that was ever supported in UAs (even if it was just in IE), then I think it’s appropriate to list is in this section.\n\nThat said, I don’t think we have to go crazy trying to put in every single element and attribute that per that rule could be a candidate for including in that section. It should just be guided by common sense.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
